CURRENT DEPENDENCY STATUS

Backend Issue A and Backend Issue B have now been implemented.

You must inspect the current local contracts and implementation and use those
new capabilities as part of #582.

Backend Issue D (server-side season/competition leaderboards) is NOT required
before starting #582.

Do not wait for Issue D and do not stop the implementation because it is
missing.

Complete all #582 work that is supported by the current backend, including:

- improved match/innings summaries;
- fixture-level batting and bowling leaders;
- batting and bowling scorecards;
- participant career statistics;
- participant competition statistics;
- participant season statistics;
- the new batting/bowling/fielding/appearance values supplied by Issue B;
- definitions and calculation details;
- correct zero/null/empty/partial states;
- responsive desktop/mobile behaviour;
- Day Match and Night Match support;
- accessibility and automated testing.

Season/competition cross-player leaderboards depend on Backend Issue D.

If Issue D is not yet implemented:
- do not fabricate leaderboard data;
- do not fetch all participants and rank them client-side;
- do not block the rest of #582;
- leave only that subsection outstanding and clearly report it in the
  completion summary.

Fixture-level match leaders do NOT depend on Issue D and must still be
implemented from the bounded fixture statistics response.

